PUBLIC SERVICES COMMITTEE
MINUTES
A meeting of the Public Services Committee was held on Tuesday, November 21, 2023, in
Committee Room 104 and via electronic meeting, starting at 12:00 p.m. Those in attendance were
as follows:
COMMITTEE MEMBERS: Bryan Cook, Chairman, Pete Layboum, Dr. Rinne, and Tom
Segrave.
vtw
%S
fl
e
AGENDA ITEMS
9.
ORDINANCE 3” READING
— Amending the Official Zoning map of the City of
Cheyenne changing the zoning classification from MUB Mixed-Use Business Emphasis to
CB Community Business for land located at Lot 2, Block 1, Sunnyside Addition,
10th
Filing.
Mr. Segrave moved to approve on 3” and final reading, seconded by Mr. Layboum. Motion carried
by unanimous voice vote.
Seth Lloyd, Planning & Development Department, provided a staff report.
Dr. Rinne joined the meeting at 12:05 p.m. following the vote on item #9.
10.
ORDINANCE
2nd READING
— Amending Subsections 6.6.3,b.3, 6.7.5.c, and 6.9.3.e of
the Unified Development Code (UDC), changing the building façade design requirements
for multifamily residential development. (POSTPONED FROM NOVEMBER 13,2023)
Dr. Rinne moved to approve on 2,d reading, seconded by Mr. Segrave. Dr. Rinne moved to amend
by substitute dated November 16, 2023, seconded by Mr. Segrave. Motion to amend carried with
Dr. Rinne and Mr. Segrave voting “YES” and Mr. Layboum voting “NO”. Main motion, as
amended, carried with Dr. Rinne and Mr. Segrave voting “YES” and Mr. Layboum voting “NO”.
Seth Lloyd, Planning & Development Department, provided a staff report and presented the
committee with two substitutes. Chairman Cook thanked staff for additional information and
committee members Rinne and Segrave commented on the item. Public comments were made by
Dan Dorsch, Habitat for humanity of Laramie County Executive Director; Ansley Mouw, Winters
Griffith Architects; Dale Steenbergen, Greater Cheyenne Chamber of Commerce President/CEO;
and Brandon Swain.
II.
ORDINANCE —2 READING
— Amending the Official Zoning Map of the City of
Cheyenne changing the zoning classification from CB Community Business and hR Iligh
Density Residential to MUB Mixed-Use Business for land located northwest of the
intersection of Dell Range Boulevard and Whitney Road. (SPONSOR
— MR. COOK)
