26.
RESOLUTION
— Granting an exception to the ‘201 Agreement’ for the owner of the
property located on a portion ofthe SW ¼ Section 13 to allow installation ofon-site sewage
holding tanks (septic system) located within Laramie County. (SPONSOR — MR. COOK)
Mr. Segrave moved to adopt, seconded by Mr. Laybourn.
Mr. Segrave moved to amend by
substitute dated November 20, 2023, seconded by Mr. Layboum. Motion to amend carried by
unanimous voice vote. Main motion, as amended carried by unanimous voice vote.
Connor White, Planning & Development Department, provided a staffreport. Bryce Dorr, Board
of Public Utilities Capital Projects Supervisor; Jennifer Escobedo, Cheyenne Laramie County
Public Health Environmental Health Director; and Scot Larson, Benchmark Engineers, P.C.;
provided additional information. Chairman Cook and committee member Segrave commented on
the item.
There being no further items for the agenda to come before the Public Services Committee, the
meeting was adjourned at 1:57 p.m.
Submitted by,
Jennifer McClelland
Executive Assistant to the Cheyenne City Council
